DimensionFunction -- an option for specifying custom dimension functions
************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        DimensionFunction => myFunction

Description
===========

This package provides a custom dimension function for probabilistically
computing the dimension, dimViaBezout.  However, in some cases this can be
substantially slower than calling the built in function dim.  Thus the user may
switch to using the built in function, or their own custom dimension function,
via the option DimensionFunction => ....

See also
========

  * *note dim: (Macaulay2Doc)dim, -- compute the Krull dimension
  * *note dimViaBezout: dimViaBezout, -- computes the dimension of the given
    ideal $I$ probabilistically

