File: RandomPoints.info, Node: ExtendField, Next: extendIdealByNonZeroMinor, Prev: dimViaBezout, Up: Top

ExtendField -- an option used to specify if extending the finite field is permissible here
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ExtendField => b
  * Inputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the base
        field is allowed to be extended

Description
===========

Various functions which produce points, or call functions which produce points,
may naturally find scheme theoretic points that are not rational over the base
field (for example, by intersecting with a random linear space).  Setting
ExtendField => true will tell the function that such points are valid.  Setting
ExtendField => false will tell the function ignore such points.  This sometimes
can slow computation, and other times can speed it up.  In some cases, points
over extended fields may also have better randomness properties for
applications.

See also
========

  * *note randomPoints: randomPoints, -- a function to find random points  in a
    variety.
  * *note findANonZeroMinor: findANonZeroMinor, -- finds a non-vanishing minor
    at some randomly chosen point
  * *note extendIdealByNonZeroMinor: extendIdealByNonZeroMinor, -- extends the
    ideal to aid finding singular locus

Functions with optional argument named ExtendField:
===================================================

  * "extendIdealByNonZeroMinor(...,ExtendField=>...)"
  * "findANonZeroMinor(...,ExtendField=>...)"
  * "randomPoints(...,ExtendField=>...)"

