projectionToHypersurface -- Generic projection to a hypersurface
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        projectionToHypersurface I
        projectionToHypersurface R
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, an ideal in a polynomial ring
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a quotient of a polynomial ring
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Codimension => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null,
        specified if you already know the codimension of your Ideal (or
        QuotientRing) in your ambient ring
      * *note MaxCoordinatesToReplace: MaxCoordinatesToReplace, => an *note
        integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, to be passed to
        randomCoordinateChange
      * *note Replacement: Replacement, => a *note symbol:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value Binomial, to be passed to
        randomCoordinateChange
      * Homogeneous => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default
        value true, to be passed to randomCoordinateChange
      * *note Verbose: genericProjection_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmVerbose=>_pd_pd_pd_rp,
        => a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false,
        set to true for verbose output
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, a list with two entries, the
        generic projection map, and the ideal if I was provided, or the ring if
        R was provided

Description
===========

This creates a projection to a hypersurface.  It differs from
genericProjection(codim I - 1, I) as it only tries to find a hypersurface
equation that vanishes along the projection, instead of finding one that
vanishes exactly at the projection.  This can be faster, and can be useful for
finding points.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ/5[x,y,z];                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(random(3,R)-2, random(2,R));                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : projectionToHypersurface(I)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|              ZZ                             6     5      4 2       5    6   |
|o3 = (map (R, --[y..z], {x, y - 2z}), ideal(y  - 2y z - 2y z  - 2y*z  + z  - |
|               5                                                             |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|       2       2                                                             |
|     2y z + y*z  - 1))                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : projectionToHypersurface(R/I)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|                                                   R                         |
|o4 = (map (------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                3       2     3    2     2        2       2     3            |
|           (- 2x  - 2x*y  - 2y  + x z - y z + 2x*z  - 2y*z  - 2z  - 2, - 2x*z|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                               ZZ                            |
|                                               --[y..z]                      |
|                                                5                            |
|     --------------, --------------------------------------------------------|
|                 2    6    5      4 2     2 4      5     3    2       2    3 |
|      + 2y*z - 2z )  y  - y z + 2y z  - 2y z  - y*z  + 2y  - y z - y*z  + z  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                                      ZZ                     |
|                                                      --[y..z]               |
|                                                       5                     |
|     ---, {y + 2z, x + z}), -------------------------------------------------|
|                             6    5      4 2     2 4      5     3    2       |
|     + 1                    y  - y z + 2y z  - 2y z  - y*z  + 2y  - y z - y*z|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     ----------)                                                             |
|     2    3                                                                  |
|       + z  + 1                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

If you already know the codimension is c, you can set Codimension=>c so the
function does not compute it.

See also
========

  * *note genericProjection: genericProjection, -- finds a random (somewhat)
    generic projection of the ring or ideal

